#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:169
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Client` from `@atproto/lex` accepts the OAuth session directly — the same way it accepts a `PasswordSession` in the [Build an Agent tutorial](/guides/bot-tutorial). From here you can `.get()`, `.list()`, `.create()`, and `.call()` any installed Lexicon.\n"
msgstr "`@atproto/lex`の`Client`はOAuthセッションを直接受け取れます。これは[エージェント作成チュートリアル](/guides/bot-tutorial)で`PasswordSession`を受け取るのと同じです。ここから先は、インストール済みLexiconに対して`.get()`、`.list()`、`.create()`、`.call()`を使えます。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:171
#, no-wrap
msgid "## Part 5: Run It\n"
msgstr "<Heading level={2} id=\"part-5-run-it\">パート5：実行する</Heading>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:173
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run your CLI tool with `npx tsx`, passing your handle as an argument:\n"
msgstr "`npx tsx`でCLIツールを実行し、引数に自分のハンドルを渡します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```bash\n"
"npx tsx src/index.ts your-handle.bsky.social\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""
"```bash\n"
"npx tsx src/index.ts your-handle.bsky.social\n"
"```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your browser should open to a consent screen. After you approve, the CLI will print your profile:\n"
msgstr "ブラウザで同意画面が開きます。承認すると、CLIがプロフィールを表示します。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:184
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"Logging in as your-handle.bsky.social...\n"
"Listening on http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback for OAuth redirect...\n"
"Logged in! DID: did:plc:xxxxx\n"
msgstr ""
"```\n"
"Logging in as your-handle.bsky.social...\n"
"Listening on http://127.0.0.1:3000/callback for OAuth redirect...\n"
"Logged in! DID: did:plc:xxxxx\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:191
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Profile:\n"
"  Handle: your-handle.bsky.social\n"
"  DID: did:plc:xxxxx\n"
"  Display name: Your Name\n"
"  Description: Your bio here\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""
"Profile:\n"
"  Handle: your-handle.bsky.social\n"
"  DID: did:plc:xxxxx\n"
"  Display name: Your Name\n"
"  Description: Your bio here\n"
"```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "You've built a minimal OAuth CLI tool that authenticates with the AT Protocol. The full source is about 80 lines of code.\n"
msgstr "ATプロトコルで認証する最小構成のOAuth CLIツールが完成しました。ソースコード全体はおよそ80行です。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/guides/oauth-cli-tutorial/en.mdx:201
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- **This is for local development.** The loopback client won't work in production — see the [OAuth with NextJS Tutorial](/guides/oauth-tutorial) for deploying a real app.\n"
"- **Sessions are in-memory.** Every run requires re-authorization. For persistent sessions, use a database as shown in the [NextJS tutorial](/guides/oauth-tutorial#part-3-adding-database-persistence).\n"
"- **Scopes.** This tutorial requests only the base `atproto` scope. To read or write data on behalf of the user, you'll need additional [scopes](/guides/scopes).\n"
msgstr ""
"- **これはローカル開発向けです**。ループバッククライアントは本番環境では動作しません。実アプリのデプロイは[OAuth with NextJSチュートリアル](/guides/oauth-tutorial)を参照してください。\n"
"- **セッションはメモリ上に保持されます**。実行のたびに再認可が必要です。永続セッションが必要な場合は、[NextJSチュートリアル](/guides/oauth-tutorial#part-3-adding-database-persistence)のようにデータベースを使ってください。\n"
"- **スコープに注意してください**。このチュートリアルが要求するのは基本の`atproto`スコープのみです。ユーザーに代わってデータを読み書きするには、追加の[スコープ](/guides/scopes)が必要です。\n"
